# Waitlist / Contact Forms with FormSubmit

Use FormSubmit.co for email-backed forms (waitlist, contact, phone signup). No backend required.

## Pattern

- **action**: `https://formsubmit.co/info@hasm.io`
- **method**: `POST`
- **Hidden fields**: `_next` (redirect URL after submit), `_subject` (email subject).

## Example

```html
<form id="waitlistForm" action="https://formsubmit.co/info@hasm.io" method="POST" aria-label="Join waitlist">
  <input type="hidden" name="_next" value="/" />
  <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="New Hasm waitlist signup" />
  <input type="tel" name="phone" placeholder="+966 5X XXX XXXX" required aria-label="Phone number" />
  <button type="submit">Send</button>
</form>
```

## JS

- Do **not** `preventDefault()` on submit when the form is valid; let it POST to FormSubmit.
- Only prevent submit when validation fails (e.g. empty required field) and call `input.focus()`.

## Notes

- Replace `_next` with a full URL (e.g. your deployed site) for redirect after submit.
- FormSubmit sends the form fields to the email in the action URL.
